  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Viyond System**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started diving into the Viyond system, which is centered around the Smart Web Scooter Booking Engine. I\'m focusing on the attached PDF and UI/UX design. I\'m excited about `VIYOND (Vision & Beyond)`! I\'m starting to build a mental map of how the web part and n8n sync work together.\n\n\n**Configuring for Client Needs**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the architecture and master template configuration. The goal is to make it easy for Beny and Dede to create customized client configurations in minutes. I\'ve been thinking about the interactive \"Master Template Configurator\" panel, allowing real-time testing of changes to brand name, colors, and API endpoints, and I\'m adding a Telegram Bot Staff Simulator!\n\nI\'m also working on the Visual Design & Layout, aiming for a Deep Blue Glass + High-Contrast Action UI that matches the SVG mockup, utilizing a gradient color scheme, crisp glassmorphic cards and clean typography. The layout needs to be responsive, and I\'m giving thought to how it will display on different devices.\n\n\n**Designing the Booking Engine**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the interactive 3-Step Booking Engine. I\'m exploring two view modes: a responsive desktop layout with live updates and a 3-screen mobile showcase mirroring the SVG design. Providing both wizard and \"All 3 Steps Board View\" will be extremely useful for client presentations. I\'m also carefully checking every detail of the 3-Step Mobile-First Booking Wizard from both the PDF and SVG design.\n\n\n**Refining the Booking Wizard**\n\nI\'m now integrating indicator tabs for clear step progression: Unit & Zone, KYC, and Payment. I\'ve drafted Step 1\'s \"Hero\" section with headlines in both English and Indonesian, and added trust signals. I\'m building a rental period selector with live duration calculation and a \"Check Live Stock\" button synced via n8n. The fleet catalog is taking shape with filtering.\n\n\n**Cataloging Vehicle Options**\n\nI\'m now detailing the fleet catalog within Step 1, starting with the scooter offerings: Yamaha NMAX, Honda PCX, Honda Scoopy, Honda Vario, and Yamaha Fazzio, each with specific details and pricing. I\'m focusing on crafting concise descriptors and availability status for each, incorporating UAT scenarios for stock management, like the PCX\'s \"Sold Out\" status, and the Telegram bot integration.\n\n\n**Defining Delivery and Terms**\n\nI\'m now detailing the hotel zone delivery options, including the zone dropdown, hotel name input, and preferred delivery time selection. I\'m also planning the bilingual rental terms, insurance, and FAQ accordion section, as well as the sticky price summary with the exact pricing formula from the PDF, including the zone cost calculation.\n\n\n**Detailing KYC Verification**\n\nI\'m now detailing Step 2, focusing on the enhanced KYC process with client-side image compression and AI-powered OCR. I\'m crafting the renter contact details fields, including name, WhatsApp number with a country code selector, and nationality, which determines eligibility for Cash on Delivery. I\'m also including four mandatory document upload slots, along with client-side image compression and one-click UAT demo presets for simulated scenarios.\n\n\n**Implementing KYC Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating the test scenario functionality within Step 2. I\'m building out options to allow the user to test real Gemini Vision OCR by uploading their own image, or using instant UAT Scenario #3 which triggers blurry photo rejection without losing form state. I\'m focusing on the four required document slots, including AI OCR checks and client-side image compression. There\'s now the addition of a mandatory UU PDP Compliance Checkbox.\n\n\n**Refining Payment Methods**\n\nI\'m now detailing Step 3: Payment. The booking summary card displays selected unit, rental dates, delivery address, a price breakdown, and total cost. I\'m focusing on the three payment methods: instant online payment, manual bank transfer, and a cash-on-delivery (COD) option. Manual Bank Transfer will require owner verification via Telegram Bot. I\'m adding a sticky validation status bar with clear \"Continue to Payment\" instructions.\n\n\n**Finalizing Confirmation Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the final booking confirmation step. This includes the `Submit and Verify My Booking` CTA which triggers the booking POST request. I\'m focusing on the live confirmation card, showing the booking status, backend actions (WhatsApp confirmation, courier sync, database lock), and the option to open WhatsApp tracking. I\'m excited about the UAT simulation, which will let me click on approval in the Owner Telegram Bot and watch the real system lock the license plate, courier task, and e-receipt!\n\n\n"
